4
00:00:05,110 --> 00:00:06,960
But every time I dream,

5
00:00:07,310 --> 00:00:08,640
it's always about her.

6
00:00:11,330 --> 00:00:13,400
I used to be in here, didn't I?

7
00:00:13,860 --> 00:00:15,920
But my feelings say otherwise.

8
00:00:16,510 --> 00:00:17,990
I kissed you,

9
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:20,400
because I don't want to be just friends.

10
00:00:21,130 --> 00:00:22,690
We still have hope.

11
00:00:23,220 --> 00:00:24,220
What hope?

12
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:25,090
Chris...

13
00:00:25,450 --> 00:00:26,980
will never love Nadear.

14
00:00:27,610 --> 00:00:30,220
I'll help you out.

15
00:00:31,340 --> 00:00:33,690
I want you to remember.

16
00:00:33,910 --> 00:00:35,550
I'll make Chris

17
00:00:35,710 --> 00:00:36,970
mine...

18
00:00:37,490 --> 00:00:39,320
by any means necessary.

19
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:45,120
[Several days ago]

20
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:46,460
She's there.

21
00:00:47,340 --> 00:00:49,110
I can't believe

22
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:52,300
that I'll get to see her again.

23
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:54,760
She seems to enjoy working out, huh?

24
00:00:55,020 --> 00:00:56,600
If she isn't swimming,

25
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:58,300
she'll usually come to this park to run.

26
00:01:00,110 --> 00:01:02,120
She really hasn't changed at all.

27
00:01:03,610 --> 00:01:04,610
It's different, though.

28
00:01:05,310 --> 00:01:06,720
She lost her memories.

29
00:01:08,710 --> 00:01:09,800
What do you think?

30
00:01:19,010 --> 00:01:20,900
Did she really forget about me?

31
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,060
She didn't keep her promise.

32
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,910
If she really has forgotten about me,

33
00:01:32,690 --> 00:01:34,410
maybe I can finally let this go.

34
00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:39,640
But I still want to make sure.

35
00:01:58,980 --> 00:02:00,040
Carissa...

36
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:02,650
You really don't remember me?

37
00:02:41,540 --> 00:02:51,460
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

38
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:56,580
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

39
00:02:56,600 --> 00:03:00,480
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

40
00:03:00,690 --> 00:03:06,690
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

41
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:16,440
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

42
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:21,500
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

43
00:03:21,520 --> 00:03:25,800
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

44
00:03:25,820 --> 00:03:34,460
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

45
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:43,280
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

46
00:04:01,760 --> 00:04:03,160
I knew what love was

47
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:06,920
when I first met you.

48
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:31,050
Her touch...

49
00:04:32,340 --> 00:04:33,840
Her smell...

50
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:06,770
Chris.

51
00:05:09,750 --> 00:05:10,990
I'll make things right

52
00:05:12,050 --> 00:05:13,290
in three months.

53
00:05:24,070 --> 00:05:24,850
Mm.

54
00:05:35,230 --> 00:05:36,850
I'll wait for you
no matter how long it takes.

55
00:05:52,680 --> 00:05:53,260
Here.

56
00:05:59,690 --> 00:06:00,770
Thanks.

57
00:06:01,130 --> 00:06:01,790
Mm.

58
00:06:04,870 --> 00:06:06,160
What will you do next?

59
00:06:08,910 --> 00:06:10,430
It's just three months.

60
00:06:11,420 --> 00:06:13,410
It's nothing compared to
the four years I've waited.

61
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:17,580
You finally got her back, huh?

62
00:06:19,670 --> 00:06:21,380
I already did it once.

63
00:06:22,060 --> 00:06:23,560
Why can't I do it again?

64
00:06:25,640 --> 00:06:27,570
If everything ends well, that's good.

65
00:06:28,090 --> 00:06:29,260
But keep in mind

66
00:06:29,570 --> 00:06:31,290
if Nadear asked her this,

67
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:33,170
it means

68
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:35,090
she's already planned
what she will do next.

69
00:06:35,870 --> 00:06:37,260
It's been four years,

70
00:06:37,700 --> 00:06:39,490
and Chris still came back to me.

71
00:06:40,210 --> 00:06:41,730
What can Nadear do?

72
00:06:42,980 --> 00:06:43,910
Hold Chris back.

73
00:06:44,570 --> 00:06:46,450
She managed to ask for three months.

74
00:06:46,610 --> 00:06:47,850
Don't you think

75
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:50,280
that maybe she can
keep asking for more time?

76
00:06:58,290 --> 00:06:59,750
Actually...

77
00:07:00,990 --> 00:07:02,490
Those three months

78
00:07:03,490 --> 00:07:05,270
aren't just important to Nadear.

79
00:07:07,870 --> 00:07:09,970
They're important to me too.

80
00:07:13,970 --> 00:07:15,440
I don't know

81
00:07:17,750 --> 00:07:19,260
if what we have between Chris and me

82
00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:22,680
is really "love,"

83
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:25,990
or just an instinct.

84
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:28,670
A feeling of nostalgia.

85
00:07:30,690 --> 00:07:31,790
So...

86
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:33,860
How are they different?

87
00:07:35,380 --> 00:07:37,060
Because Chris lost her memories.

88
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:42,990
If our love

89
00:07:43,250 --> 00:07:46,000
came from familiarity,

90
00:07:49,350 --> 00:07:51,480
Chris might not choose me.

91
00:07:58,980 --> 00:08:00,660
If over these three months,

92
00:08:03,210 --> 00:08:05,450
our love blooms once more...

93
00:08:07,090 --> 00:08:09,280
If it really is love,

94
00:08:12,970 --> 00:08:14,980
I won't care about her past again.

95
00:08:29,690 --> 00:08:31,360
Are you having a sleepover
with your friends?

96
00:08:31,730 --> 00:08:32,360
Mm.

97
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:33,720
That way, I'll get to leave my room.

98
00:08:34,370 --> 00:08:37,010
Tell your friends that you want to
spend some time with your girlfriend.

99
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:41,010
They'll think I'm avoiding them.

100
00:08:45,390 --> 00:08:46,930
You worry about what your friends think,

101
00:08:47,910 --> 00:08:49,780
but you don't worry
if your girlfriend misses you?

102
00:08:51,340 --> 00:08:53,920
Her hair smells faintly of shampoo.

103
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:55,330
Her hair is fine

104
00:08:55,770 --> 00:08:57,130
and smooth.

105
00:08:59,880 --> 00:09:02,760
She likes to tuck it behind
her ears to keep it out of her face

106
00:09:03,660 --> 00:09:05,570
when she bends down
to kiss me on the bed.

107
00:09:15,870 --> 00:09:16,570
Sun...

108
00:09:19,380 --> 00:09:20,190
Sun.

109
00:09:25,810 --> 00:09:26,770
Who is that?

110
00:09:32,860 --> 00:09:34,260
How did you get in here?

111
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:38,770
I was worried you might have
a nightmare,

112
00:09:39,150 --> 00:09:41,610
so I came in to check on you as usual.

113
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:45,250
But what's happening
between us isn't usual.

114
00:09:45,950 --> 00:09:48,480
But we still have three months to
get back to how it used to be.

115
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:55,810
And who is Sun?

116
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:01,860
A friend.

117
00:10:06,160 --> 00:10:08,760
A friend who helped me come up
with the flower dishes.

118
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:12,840
I think you're so stressed
about the flower dishes

119
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:18,750
that you even dreamed about your friend.

120
00:10:23,050 --> 00:10:24,510
I think you should rest.

121
00:10:28,460 --> 00:10:29,760
Rest?

122
00:10:30,460 --> 00:10:31,240
Your work.

123
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:34,860
Stop doing your work.

124
00:10:50,010 --> 00:10:51,880
You've treated me like a sick person

125
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:54,440
for four whole years.

126
00:10:54,700 --> 00:10:56,760
Hasn't that been more than enough?

127
00:10:57,970 --> 00:10:59,640
- I'm just...
- "Worried."

128
00:11:00,460 --> 00:11:01,460
"Want what's best for me."

129
00:11:02,570 --> 00:11:04,800
I've heard you say this
hundreds of times now.

130
00:11:06,130 --> 00:11:08,020
You want me to act normal,

131
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:11,760
but don't you realize our relationship
was never normal to begin with?

132
00:11:29,930 --> 00:11:31,160
I'm going to see my friend.

133
00:11:40,770 --> 00:11:41,360
Here.

134
00:11:41,560 --> 00:11:42,470
Thanks.

135
00:11:44,930 --> 00:11:46,400
Everything is going smoothly.

136
00:11:46,420 --> 00:11:47,790
It should open on schedule.

137
00:11:49,090 --> 00:11:50,260
Well done.

138
00:11:54,430 --> 00:11:55,920
So when are you opening?

139
00:11:56,620 --> 00:11:58,140
Well, you said three more months.

140
00:12:03,190 --> 00:12:04,520
I know.

141
00:12:05,670 --> 00:12:07,780
I see you barely smiled today.

142
00:12:09,160 --> 00:12:10,670
You seem stressed.

143
00:12:11,500 --> 00:12:13,270
Is something bothering you?

144
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:17,360
It's about my dream.

145
00:12:19,450 --> 00:12:20,960
Would you like to talk about it?

146
00:12:23,130 --> 00:12:23,960
Not yet.

147
00:12:25,630 --> 00:12:26,460
Alright,

148
00:12:27,570 --> 00:12:29,060
as long as you're happy.

149
00:12:31,260 --> 00:12:32,200
Okay.

150
00:12:34,440 --> 00:12:35,760
[Verity Skin Clinic]

151
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:38,240
If I want to talk, I'll tell you.

152
00:12:38,770 --> 00:12:39,380
Mm.

153
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:49,260
So it's really you, Sun.

154
00:12:52,570 --> 00:12:55,410
[Third Person]

155
00:12:56,570 --> 00:13:00,420
[Third Person]

156
00:13:02,850 --> 00:13:04,620
Sun, your junior.

157
00:13:05,220 --> 00:13:07,090
How was she doing

158
00:13:09,120 --> 00:13:10,480
after that accident four years ago?

159
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:12,800
Her brain injury

160
00:13:13,410 --> 00:13:16,290
caused her to lose her memory temporarily.

161
00:13:16,760 --> 00:13:17,410
Does this mean

162
00:13:18,280 --> 00:13:19,210
she'll get better

163
00:13:19,410 --> 00:13:21,180
soon, right?

164
00:13:21,410 --> 00:13:22,120
Yes.

165
00:13:23,660 --> 00:13:24,940
But...

166
00:13:26,420 --> 00:13:27,630
We found that

167
00:13:28,300 --> 00:13:30,330
Sun has a tumor near her brainstem.

168
00:13:42,670 --> 00:13:44,250
When I first told you this,

169
00:13:45,140 --> 00:13:47,440
you said you were Sun's friend, didn't you?

170
00:13:47,710 --> 00:13:48,500
Yes,

171
00:13:50,160 --> 00:13:52,420
we went to the same high school.

172
00:13:54,140 --> 00:13:55,210
It's been four years.

173
00:13:56,410 --> 00:13:57,720
Why did you come back

174
00:13:57,740 --> 00:13:58,740
to ask me about this again?

175
00:13:59,150 --> 00:14:01,020
Back then, you said Sun's father

176
00:14:01,040 --> 00:14:03,010
took her overseas.

177
00:14:03,750 --> 00:14:04,520
Yes,

178
00:14:06,130 --> 00:14:07,810
she lost her memories,

179
00:14:09,750 --> 00:14:11,100
so her father took the opportunity

180
00:14:11,520 --> 00:14:13,220
to start her life anew over there.

181
00:14:15,070 --> 00:14:16,600
I think Sun got her memories back.

182
00:14:17,410 --> 00:14:18,930
If she's back...

183
00:14:21,830 --> 00:14:23,430
If she got her memories back and came back,

184
00:14:24,070 --> 00:14:26,170
why did no one know this?

185
00:14:35,830 --> 00:14:37,220
You feel like...

186
00:14:37,240 --> 00:14:38,980
you've known someone before?

187
00:14:41,710 --> 00:14:43,110
If you like someone,

188
00:14:43,510 --> 00:14:45,310
you can feel that way too.

189
00:14:46,170 --> 00:14:47,100
It's like...

190
00:14:50,310 --> 00:14:51,900
you've known each other
for a long time.

191
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:53,920
You've heard of it before, yeah?

192
00:14:56,700 --> 00:14:58,110
I think so too.

193
00:15:01,370 --> 00:15:02,400
That means you like her.

194
00:15:09,870 --> 00:15:10,910
I told you,

195
00:15:11,710 --> 00:15:13,090
I'm trying to uphold

196
00:15:13,530 --> 00:15:14,840
both my medical ethics

197
00:15:15,420 --> 00:15:16,420
and my code as a friend.

198
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:23,590
I've felt that way ever since
I first met her.

199
00:15:26,160 --> 00:15:27,850
What made you curious about this?

200
00:15:28,570 --> 00:15:29,800
I had a dream.

201
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:33,370
And I started dreaming more
as we had more physical contact.

202
00:15:33,940 --> 00:15:35,010
What are you curious about?

203
00:15:36,180 --> 00:15:38,010
Well, if I used to know her...

204
00:15:38,870 --> 00:15:40,420
What was our relationship like?

205
00:15:43,850 --> 00:15:44,900
Would you like me to help?

206
00:15:49,270 --> 00:15:50,310
I don't know...

207
00:15:51,230 --> 00:15:52,730
It feels so familiar.

208
00:15:53,910 --> 00:15:56,700
Familiar enough that I want to
find the answer myself.

209
00:16:22,430 --> 00:16:23,430
Why...

210
00:16:24,610 --> 00:16:26,500
Why can't I find anything...?

211
00:16:33,580 --> 00:16:34,840
What are you looking for?

212
00:16:38,030 --> 00:16:39,650
Are you looking for someone named Sun?

213
00:16:44,660 --> 00:16:46,010
Did you know

214
00:16:47,330 --> 00:16:49,520
why I'm suspicious of you?

215
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:57,320
Because you dreamed,

216
00:17:01,270 --> 00:17:02,900
but it wasn't the same.

217
00:17:31,390 --> 00:17:32,220
Nadear...

218
00:17:40,030 --> 00:17:41,030
Are you tired?

219
00:17:42,100 --> 00:17:43,610
Not that much.

220
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:45,790
Thank you.

221
00:17:45,810 --> 00:17:46,630
Let me massage you.

222
00:17:47,230 --> 00:17:48,110
Yes,

223
00:17:48,800 --> 00:17:51,820
back then, when I dreamed
about our past,

224
00:17:52,250 --> 00:17:54,710
I'd love Nadear even more.

225
00:17:58,730 --> 00:18:00,010
I dreamed...

226
00:18:05,150 --> 00:18:06,400
but it wasn't the same?

227
00:18:07,910 --> 00:18:10,210
Can you make an effort

228
00:18:11,610 --> 00:18:14,420
for these three months we still have?

229
00:18:44,390 --> 00:18:45,820
My clinic is ready.

230
00:18:45,840 --> 00:18:47,510
Would you like to come see it?

231
00:19:01,510 --> 00:19:04,000
Why do you want to open
a beauty clinic?

232
00:19:04,630 --> 00:19:06,410
I thought you wanted to be
a doctor and treat people.

233
00:19:07,020 --> 00:19:09,210
Why do you think I like you?

234
00:19:12,220 --> 00:19:13,850
It's because you're beautiful.

235
00:19:14,430 --> 00:19:15,290
What?

236
00:19:15,720 --> 00:19:17,580
You like me because
of how I look?

237
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:23,690
Mm.

238
00:19:25,520 --> 00:19:28,490
I want you to be my beautiful forever.

239
00:19:34,010 --> 00:19:37,660
Then...can I be your only
VIP customer forever?

240
00:19:38,690 --> 00:19:39,380
Mm.

241
00:19:40,070 --> 00:19:41,020
Forever.

242
00:20:49,730 --> 00:20:52,710
I'm your first love, Chris.

243
00:20:58,310 --> 00:20:59,600
What does that mean?

244
00:21:01,830 --> 00:21:05,170
It's a way to bring you back
to who you used to be.

245
00:21:06,940 --> 00:21:09,360
I never liked it, though.

246
00:21:11,610 --> 00:21:13,470
I don't like it either.

247
00:21:16,610 --> 00:21:18,420
But it's for your own good.

248
00:21:22,710 --> 00:21:24,000
You know

249
00:21:24,020 --> 00:21:26,910
I'm willing to do anything for you.

250
00:21:28,910 --> 00:21:30,990
What do you smell?

251
00:21:32,710 --> 00:21:33,710
Roses...

252
00:21:35,620 --> 00:21:36,900
And...

253
00:21:37,240 --> 00:21:39,250
Where are you right now?

254
00:21:40,990 --> 00:21:42,220
School...

255
00:21:43,810 --> 00:21:45,810
What are you doing?

256
00:21:47,130 --> 00:21:49,620
Copying my friend's homework.

257
00:21:50,480 --> 00:21:52,410
So why did you smell roses?

258
00:21:58,520 --> 00:21:59,240
Here.

259
00:22:01,520 --> 00:22:02,850
Did you buy these to give to people?

260
00:22:03,360 --> 00:22:04,110
No,

261
00:22:04,130 --> 00:22:05,310
they're offerings for Buddha.

262
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:09,020
Then no thanks. I don't want to
take one meant for Buddha.

263
00:22:11,060 --> 00:22:12,730
This one isn't an offering.

264
00:22:13,560 --> 00:22:15,180
I want to give it to you.

265
00:22:16,750 --> 00:22:18,080
She gave it to me

266
00:22:18,290 --> 00:22:20,360
before Buddhism class.

267
00:22:34,290 --> 00:22:35,290
Hey, wait!

268
00:22:35,950 --> 00:22:36,690
Chris!

269
00:22:48,820 --> 00:22:50,540
Have you finished copying my homework?

270
00:22:51,380 --> 00:22:53,110
Not yet. Are you going to turn it in now?

271
00:22:53,860 --> 00:22:54,660
It's alright.

272
00:22:54,680 --> 00:22:56,000
I'll wait until you're done.

273
00:22:56,720 --> 00:22:57,650
Give me a sec.

274
00:23:06,580 --> 00:23:07,730
Sun...

275
00:23:09,910 --> 00:23:11,030
is my friend...?

276
00:23:22,720 --> 00:23:23,530
What's wrong?

277
00:23:30,110 --> 00:23:33,850
[Third Person]

278
00:23:36,140 --> 00:23:38,860
[Third Person]

279
00:23:42,090 --> 00:23:43,170
Jeen.

280
00:23:47,290 --> 00:23:48,100
Chris.

281
00:23:49,840 --> 00:23:50,550
I think

282
00:23:50,950 --> 00:23:52,160
Chris needs to rest.

283
00:24:01,760 --> 00:24:02,760
Sun...

284
00:24:03,330 --> 00:24:04,370
Sun.

285
00:24:06,270 --> 00:24:07,270
Chris,

286
00:24:09,070 --> 00:24:12,350
will you stop hurting yourself
because of that woman?

287
00:24:23,570 --> 00:24:25,420
Nadear, I'm at your front door.

288
00:24:25,440 --> 00:24:26,830
We should talk.

289
00:24:27,100 --> 00:24:28,540
Four years ago,

290
00:24:29,040 --> 00:24:30,820
Chris's symptoms were very severe,

291
00:24:31,300 --> 00:24:32,950
so you asked me

292
00:24:33,560 --> 00:24:36,160
to help Chris live normally.

293
00:24:41,080 --> 00:24:41,850
Yes,

294
00:24:42,760 --> 00:24:44,640
you helped both Chris

295
00:24:44,870 --> 00:24:46,070
and me.

296
00:24:48,310 --> 00:24:49,450
Back then, Chris's brain

297
00:24:49,480 --> 00:24:52,380
was like a clear, empty glass.

298
00:24:53,430 --> 00:24:55,400
Whatever color we add,

299
00:24:55,730 --> 00:24:57,460
that's what we'll see.

300
00:25:00,130 --> 00:25:02,560
What are you implying?

301
00:25:03,690 --> 00:25:06,610
Chris now has her own memories.

302
00:25:08,190 --> 00:25:09,800
I'm not sure

303
00:25:10,080 --> 00:25:11,650
her body can handle it

304
00:25:12,300 --> 00:25:13,940
if we still keep this up.

305
00:25:15,440 --> 00:25:17,300
All of Chris's memories

306
00:25:18,020 --> 00:25:19,510
are too much

307
00:25:19,530 --> 00:25:21,540
for the same clear glass to hold.

308
00:25:22,470 --> 00:25:25,340
If remembering everything hurts her,

309
00:25:27,140 --> 00:25:30,180
then I want her to remember that much.

310
00:25:35,250 --> 00:25:37,860
I can't afford to lose her again.

311
00:26:00,290 --> 00:26:02,350
Any updates on the flower dishes?

312
00:26:09,990 --> 00:26:12,460
Chris is unwell. I'll tell you later.

313
00:27:04,270 --> 00:27:05,320
Chris,

314
00:27:05,340 --> 00:27:06,750
are you alright?

315
00:27:07,270 --> 00:27:08,940
I'm in front of your house.

316
00:27:09,440 --> 00:27:10,700
Can you come see me?

317
00:27:15,180 --> 00:27:16,530
[Chris, are you alright?]

318
00:27:16,560 --> 00:27:17,680
[I'm in front of your house.
Can you come see me?]

319
00:27:44,460 --> 00:27:46,780
This really looks like we're
having an affair.

320
00:27:48,740 --> 00:27:50,360
Why were you gone, then?

321
00:27:50,520 --> 00:27:51,860
I couldn't contact you.

322
00:27:54,500 --> 00:27:55,850
I'm sick.

323
00:28:01,470 --> 00:28:02,680
You don't have a fever, though.

324
00:28:05,920 --> 00:28:07,800
I'm a bit dizzy and nauseous.

325
00:28:08,710 --> 00:28:10,860
There is a lot to think
about right now,

326
00:28:10,880 --> 00:28:12,360
so it's affecting my body.

327
00:28:15,300 --> 00:28:16,680
Did you think about me too?

328
00:28:20,070 --> 00:28:20,960
Yeah.

329
00:28:22,400 --> 00:28:23,150
Come on,

330
00:28:23,170 --> 00:28:24,370
I thought you'd flirt back

331
00:28:24,990 --> 00:28:25,950
and say, "I missed you."

332
00:28:28,400 --> 00:28:29,400
Sorry,

333
00:28:29,650 --> 00:28:31,940
I'm a bit out of it right now.

334
00:28:32,560 --> 00:28:33,840
I couldn't come up with that in time.

335
00:28:37,560 --> 00:28:38,760
Is it related to your brain?

336
00:28:41,930 --> 00:28:42,860
Yeah.

337
00:28:43,370 --> 00:28:44,880
I used to have amnesia.

338
00:28:46,090 --> 00:28:48,020
I still can't remember everything,

339
00:28:48,980 --> 00:28:50,580
but it's like...

340
00:28:51,030 --> 00:28:53,050
my memories are coming back.

341
00:28:56,360 --> 00:28:58,070
Would you like to remember?

342
00:29:00,770 --> 00:29:01,870
I don't know.

343
00:29:03,530 --> 00:29:05,560
Both trying to remember

344
00:29:05,700 --> 00:29:08,250
and not being able to remember

345
00:29:09,680 --> 00:29:11,300
make me suffer.

346
00:29:18,630 --> 00:29:19,950
Why don't you stop thinking about it?

347
00:29:47,460 --> 00:29:49,730
If you're happy with how things are now,

348
00:29:50,860 --> 00:29:52,450
why not just stay in the present?

349
00:29:55,430 --> 00:29:57,350
You really think so?

350
00:29:58,240 --> 00:29:59,070
Mm.

351
00:29:59,960 --> 00:30:02,360
I lost my dog, whom I loved dearly.

352
00:30:04,130 --> 00:30:05,760
My friend felt bad for me,

353
00:30:06,360 --> 00:30:08,370
so they gave me a replica dog.

354
00:30:10,590 --> 00:30:11,940
When I saw it,

355
00:30:12,160 --> 00:30:13,560
it made me even sadder

356
00:30:15,570 --> 00:30:17,270
because it reminded me

357
00:30:17,750 --> 00:30:19,570
that I'd already lost my dog.

358
00:30:20,630 --> 00:30:21,630
A dog?

359
00:30:21,970 --> 00:30:22,970
What was their name?

360
00:30:25,270 --> 00:30:26,660
"Kiiro."

361
00:30:31,200 --> 00:30:32,260
Kiiro?

362
00:30:34,230 --> 00:30:35,200
Yes,

363
00:30:35,230 --> 00:30:36,470
it means "yellow."

364
00:30:39,520 --> 00:30:41,070
My fish is also named "Kiiro."

365
00:30:50,150 --> 00:30:51,060
Sun,

366
00:30:52,820 --> 00:30:54,370
have we known each other before?

367
00:31:41,660 --> 00:31:42,440
Nadear.

368
00:31:51,190 --> 00:31:53,350
Why did you go
outside without telling me?

369
00:31:56,320 --> 00:31:57,940
I just wanted to take a walk.

370
00:32:01,750 --> 00:32:02,820
Get some rest.

371
00:32:16,480 --> 00:32:19,260
We still have three months, don't we?

372
00:32:21,460 --> 00:32:23,060
Less than three months.

373
00:32:36,090 --> 00:32:37,240
Look at you.

374
00:32:37,460 --> 00:32:39,320
You don't want to be
a pretty doctor, huh?

375
00:32:40,780 --> 00:32:42,680
I'm still pretty.

376
00:32:43,630 --> 00:32:44,260
Yeah, yeah.

377
00:32:45,020 --> 00:32:46,300
Why did you do that?

378
00:32:46,700 --> 00:32:49,020
Just say the truth
and everything will be resolved.

379
00:32:49,780 --> 00:32:51,850
I don't understand.
Why didn't you tell her?

380
00:32:53,860 --> 00:32:56,240
Because the fact that Chris loves me

381
00:32:57,210 --> 00:33:00,980
doesn't make what I did right.

382
00:33:01,710 --> 00:33:03,160
You weren't the only one at fault.

383
00:33:03,770 --> 00:33:06,420
If her memories hurt her...

384
00:33:08,080 --> 00:33:09,960
The only thing I want right now

385
00:33:12,160 --> 00:33:13,780
is for her to love me.

386
00:33:18,740 --> 00:33:20,460
If she loves me,

387
00:33:20,780 --> 00:33:23,100
I'll tell her what we used to be.

388
00:33:25,620 --> 00:33:27,420
I want to be sure

389
00:33:29,100 --> 00:33:30,850
that she will forgive me first.

390
00:33:36,320 --> 00:33:37,360
Alright.

391
00:33:43,920 --> 00:33:47,120
[Third Person]

392
00:33:48,030 --> 00:33:52,120
[Third Person]

393
00:34:06,880 --> 00:34:07,730
Nadear...

394
00:34:30,390 --> 00:34:32,010
Chris betrayed me.

395
00:34:34,540 --> 00:34:37,720
She betrayed me again, Jeen.

396
00:34:52,500 --> 00:34:54,840
I lost my dog, whom I loved dearly.

397
00:34:56,130 --> 00:34:57,200
A dog?

398
00:34:57,430 --> 00:34:58,430
What was their name?

399
00:35:00,780 --> 00:35:02,020
Kiiro.

400
00:35:12,830 --> 00:35:15,430
Did your name come from
the word "yellow" as well?

401
00:35:16,020 --> 00:35:17,120
Kiiro.

402
00:35:36,260 --> 00:35:36,890
Kiiro...

403
00:35:36,910 --> 00:35:38,210
Kiiro is hungry.

404
00:35:38,430 --> 00:35:39,430
Come on.

405
00:35:41,650 --> 00:35:42,430
Go.

406
00:35:43,020 --> 00:35:45,020
Time to eat. Let's go.

407
00:36:16,890 --> 00:36:17,910
Nadear...

408
00:36:19,340 --> 00:36:20,340
Kiiro...

409
00:36:32,540 --> 00:36:33,990
Chris, come eat your breakfast.

410
00:36:34,140 --> 00:36:35,820
I made some for you, too.

411
00:36:37,920 --> 00:36:38,620
Thanks.

412
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:42,030
Don't forget to take your
medicine after your meal.

413
00:36:47,220 --> 00:36:48,220
Nadear,

414
00:36:50,140 --> 00:36:51,790
where did our dog go?

415
00:36:54,830 --> 00:36:56,240
What dog?

416
00:36:57,330 --> 00:36:58,730
Our dog.

417
00:36:59,230 --> 00:37:01,920
I remember we used to have a dog.

418
00:37:05,180 --> 00:37:06,820
Chris, we've never had a dog.

419
00:37:11,600 --> 00:37:12,720
We have.

420
00:37:13,230 --> 00:37:14,710
Our dog...

421
00:37:15,670 --> 00:37:16,920
The other Kiiro.

422
00:37:23,990 --> 00:37:24,840
Chris.

423
00:37:27,230 --> 00:37:28,410
Listen to me.

424
00:37:30,920 --> 00:37:32,610
We've never had a dog.

425
00:37:37,120 --> 00:37:39,810
The only possibility is that dog.

426
00:37:45,570 --> 00:37:48,340
Nan once asked us
to take care of her Corgi.

427
00:37:49,690 --> 00:37:51,920
Its fur is brown and white.

428
00:37:52,610 --> 00:37:54,800
She left it with us
when she flew overseas.

429
00:37:56,500 --> 00:37:57,600
It's smart,

430
00:37:57,620 --> 00:37:58,720
affectionate,

431
00:37:59,400 --> 00:38:01,530
and it likes sitting on your lap.

432
00:38:05,460 --> 00:38:06,720
Was it Nan's dog?

433
00:38:10,140 --> 00:38:11,030
Yeah.

434
00:38:20,820 --> 00:38:22,680
I'll go to the restaurant today, then.

435
00:38:25,030 --> 00:38:25,760
Don't.

436
00:38:25,780 --> 00:38:27,220
I want you to rest.

437
00:39:00,630 --> 00:39:01,350
So this is what

438
00:39:01,470 --> 00:39:03,320
you want me to do?

439
00:39:04,930 --> 00:39:06,410
To give Chris freedom?

440
00:39:08,450 --> 00:39:10,630
To let Chris love someone else?

441
00:39:13,780 --> 00:39:16,410
I don't know what to do anymore, Jeen.

442
00:39:18,340 --> 00:39:21,730
Even her memories don't
seem to be enough to make her mine.

443
00:39:24,330 --> 00:39:26,230
Our brains are complex.

444
00:39:28,500 --> 00:39:30,220
Chris remembers you,

445
00:39:30,450 --> 00:39:32,010
but she still had an affair.

446
00:39:33,170 --> 00:39:34,530
Perhaps...

447
00:39:34,810 --> 00:39:36,610
her memories alone aren't enough.

448
00:39:38,480 --> 00:39:39,810
You first have to know

449
00:39:40,020 --> 00:39:41,710
what Chris is planning to do.

450
00:39:44,340 --> 00:39:46,920
If I do, Chris will be mine again, right?

451
00:40:27,840 --> 00:40:29,230
Welcome, Chris.

452
00:40:30,410 --> 00:40:32,110
Can I stay with you tonight?

453
00:40:33,310 --> 00:40:35,440
My place is your place.

454
00:40:50,950 --> 00:40:52,330
Should I change my hairstyle?

455
00:40:53,420 --> 00:40:54,420
Why?

456
00:40:55,920 --> 00:40:57,210
I want to be a new me.

457
00:40:59,560 --> 00:41:00,930
No need to do that.

458
00:41:01,580 --> 00:41:03,020
I like you just the way you are.

459
00:41:06,020 --> 00:41:07,120
Thanks.

460
00:41:15,830 --> 00:41:17,390
We're friends, so let's stop here.

461
00:41:20,310 --> 00:41:22,430
But we've gone a lot further than this.

462
00:41:27,500 --> 00:41:30,200
If you realize that, then you should
keep a proper distance.

463
00:41:33,010 --> 00:41:34,020
Okay.

464
00:41:36,340 --> 00:41:38,160
Tonight...

465
00:41:39,060 --> 00:41:40,180
Let's just hold hands.

466
00:41:51,810 --> 00:41:53,130
Just hold hands.

467
00:41:54,150 --> 00:41:55,910
Well, I'm just holding your hand,

468
00:41:56,260 --> 00:41:57,510
nothing more.

469
00:42:00,800 --> 00:42:02,920
But isn't this too close?

470
00:42:04,090 --> 00:42:05,620
Friends can be this close.

471
00:42:28,190 --> 00:42:29,190
This is weird.

472
00:42:29,210 --> 00:42:31,110
Why did you suddenly
ask me to meet you in private?

473
00:42:31,130 --> 00:42:32,710
Didn't Nadear say you were sick?

474
00:42:34,010 --> 00:42:35,420
Have you ever had a dog?

475
00:42:36,930 --> 00:42:38,040
A Corgi.

476
00:42:39,230 --> 00:42:40,590
I'm a cat person.

477
00:42:40,620 --> 00:42:42,120
I've never had a dog before.

478
00:42:57,730 --> 00:42:58,730
Kiiro.

479
00:42:59,330 --> 00:43:00,510
Whose dog is it?

480
00:43:22,840 --> 00:43:25,470
I don't think it's true that
we've never known each other before.

481
00:43:25,630 --> 00:43:26,520
Kiiro.

482
00:43:26,570 --> 00:43:28,160
It's not a coincidence, right?

483
00:43:28,310 --> 00:43:30,030
I just want to know the truth.

484
00:43:30,220 --> 00:43:31,540
Who I am right now

485
00:43:31,560 --> 00:43:32,680
is the truth.

486
00:43:32,920 --> 00:43:34,530
Ever since I lost my memories...

487
00:43:34,860 --> 00:43:37,200
Love was just attachment.

488
00:43:37,280 --> 00:43:38,540
We should break up.

489
00:43:38,560 --> 00:43:40,410
Whoever dares to take
Chris away from me

490
00:43:40,430 --> 00:43:41,720
will die.

491
00:43:41,830 --> 00:43:43,400
To overcome your fear,

492
00:43:43,420 --> 00:43:44,600
you'll have to face it.

493
00:43:44,730 --> 00:43:46,410
I'll be with you.

494
00:44:01,820 --> 00:44:11,740
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

495
00:44:11,760 --> 00:44:16,860
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

496
00:44:16,880 --> 00:44:20,760
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

497
00:44:20,980 --> 00:44:26,980
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

498
00:44:27,000 --> 00:44:36,720
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

499
00:44:36,740 --> 00:44:41,780
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

500
00:44:41,800 --> 00:44:46,080
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

501
00:44:46,100 --> 00:44:54,740
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

502
00:44:55,260 --> 00:45:03,560
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫
